window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-fc9fbba758a53038"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"use-chatgpt-work-and-codex-with-amazon-bedrock\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt-work-codex-amazon-bedrock\">在 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 中使用 Amazon Bedrock</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>配置本地 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 客户端，让它们通过 Amazon Bedrock 使用 OpenAI 模型。在此配置中，本地客户端使用 AWS 管理的身份验证和访问控制，将模型请求发送到 Bedrock。</p> <p>本文介绍直接连接 Bedrock。如果组织已提供模型网关，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">使用 API／提供方凭据</a>；若要配置由 Bedrock 提供支持的网关，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4\">通过 LiteLLM 接入 Bedrock</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-it-works\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">工作原理</h2> <p>当你把本地 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 客户端的模型提供方配置为 Amazon Bedrock 时，请求不会经过 OpenAI 托管的 Responses API。本地客户端会将模型请求发送到 Amazon Bedrock；对于受支持的 OpenAI 模型，Bedrock 提供兼容 OpenAI 的 Responses API 实现。</p> <p>身份验证由 AWS 原生机制负责。用户使用 Bedrock API 密钥或 AWS IAM 凭证进行身份验证；此提供方不使用 ChatGPT 登录，也不使用 <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">开始之前</h2> <p>请确保你具备：</p> <ul> <li>要使用的 AWS 账户凭证</li> <li>在 Amazon Bedrock 中访问受支持 OpenAI 模型的权限</li> <li>所选模型在其中可用的 AWS 区域</li> <li>调用所选模型或推理配置文件所需的 AWS 权限</li> </ul> <p>请核对每个模型对应的 IAM 要求。例如，通过 Runtime 使用 GPT-6 Sol 时，还需要对账户的默认项目拥有 <code>bedrock:InvokeModel</code> 权限。请参阅 AWS 的 <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-6-sol.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GPT-6 Sol 设置说明（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-the-provider\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">配置提供方</h2> <p>在 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 中设置 <code>model_provider</code>，即可配置 Codex 的模型提供方。ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI、IDE 扩展和 SDK 会读取相同的本地配置层。</p> <p>根据你要使用的 Amazon Bedrock 端点选择提供方：跨区域推理 (CRIS) 使用 Bedrock Runtime；区域内推理使用 Bedrock Mantle。</p> <p>新配置请使用 Bedrock Runtime：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock-runtime\"\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n</code></pre> <p>Bedrock Runtime 不支持托管网页搜索。如果需要此功能，请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=use-mantle-for-hosted-web-search\">Bedrock Mantle</a>。<code>amazon-bedrock</code> 提供方选择 Mantle；<code>amazon-bedrock-runtime</code> 提供方选择 Runtime。</p> <p><a id=\"use-mantle-for-hosted-web-search\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"mantle\">使用 Mantle 托管网页搜索</h3> <p>对于 Bedrock Mantle 端点：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock\"\nweb_search = \"cached\"\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"choose-a-model\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">选择模型</h3> <p>Codex 会根据已配置的 <code>model_provider</code> 决定模型选择器中显示哪些模型：<code>amazon-bedrock-runtime</code> 对应 Bedrock Runtime 端点支持的模型；<code>amazon-bedrock</code> 对应 Bedrock Mantle 端点支持的模型。</p> <p>你也可以在配置文件中选择性地指定一个<a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=supported-models\">受支持的模型</a>。内置提供方会提供自己的模型目录。切换端点时，请同时更改提供方和任何显式指定的模型 ID。</p> <p>模型在不同 AWS 区域的可用情况可能不同。请参阅 AWS 的<a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-region-compatibility.html#model-regions-openai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">按模型查看区域可用性（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"authentication-options\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">身份验证选项</h2> <p>本地 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 客户端支持两种 Bedrock 身份验证方式，并按以下顺序检查：</p> <ol> <li>Bedrock API 密钥</li> <li>AWS SDK 凭证链</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"option-1-bedrock-api-key\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1bedrock-api\">方式 1：Bedrock API 密钥</h3> <p>在本地客户端会读取的环境中设置 Bedrock API 密钥。使用 API 密钥身份验证时，必须指定区域。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">export AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=&lt;your-bedrock-api-key&gt;\nexport AWS_REGION=us-east-2\n</code></pre> <p>在 Windows PowerShell 中：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">$env:AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK = \"&lt;your-bedrock-api-key&gt;\"\n$env:AWS_REGION = \"us-east-2\"\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"option-2-aws-sdk-credentials\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2aws-sdk\">方式 2：AWS SDK 凭证</h3> <p>如果组织通过 AWS SDK 凭证链管理 Bedrock 访问权限，请使用此方式。本地客户端可以使用以下标准 AWS SDK 凭证来源：</p> <p><a id=\"shared-aws-configuration-files\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"aws\">共享 AWS 配置文件</h4> <p>配置共享的 AWS <code>config</code> 和 <code>credentials</code> 文件：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">aws configure\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"environment-variables\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_6\">环境变量</h4> <p>设置标准 AWS SDK 凭证环境变量：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=&lt;your-access-key-id&gt;\nexport AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=&lt;your-secret-access-key&gt;\nexport AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=&lt;your-session-token&gt;\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"aws-management-console-credentials\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"aws_1\">AWS 管理控制台凭证</h4> <p>使用 AWS 管理控制台凭证登录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">aws login\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"aws-sso-or-a-named-profile\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"aws-sso\">AWS SSO 或命名配置文件</h4> <p>使用 AWS SSO 登录并选择命名配置文件：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">aws sso login --profile codex-bedrock\nexport AWS_PROFILE=codex-bedrock\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"federated-identity\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_7\">联合身份</h4> <p>对于企业 SSO 或 OIDC 联合身份验证，请在本地客户端之外配置联合身份，并通过 <code>credential_process</code> 让 AWS SDK 解析凭证。将浏览器登录、令牌交换、缓存和刷新操作放在 AWS 配置文件的 <code>credential_process</code> 辅助程序中。</p> <p><a id=\"desktop-app-and-ide-extension\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"ide\">桌面应用和 IDE 扩展</h2> <p>桌面应用和 IDE 扩展可能无法继承 shell 中的环境变量。请将所需值放入 <code>~/.codex/.env</code>；在 Windows 上，默认路径为 <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\.env</code>。然后重启应用或扩展。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">export AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=&lt;your-bedrock-api-key&gt;\nexport AWS_REGION=us-east-2\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"verify-setup\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">验证配置</h2> <ul> <li>在 Codex CLI 中打开 <code>/status</code>，确认模型提供方与端点相符：Mantle 区域内推理应为 <code>amazon-bedrock</code>；Runtime Global 或 Geo 跨区域推理应为 <code>amazon-bedrock-runtime</code>。</li> <li>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中选择 Work 或 Codex，并在重启应用后开始一个新任务。</li> <li>在 IDE 扩展中重启扩展后开始一个新会话。</li> <li>确认所选模型在已配置的 AWS 区域中可用，并且 AWS 身份有权访问该模型。</li> </ul> <p>然后在新任务中发送一条简短提示：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Reply with exactly: bedrock-ok\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">只回复以下确切内容：bedrock-ok</div></div> <p>预期回复为 <code>bedrock-ok</code>。请在客户端中确认所用的提供方和模型；仅凭回复内容无法判断请求实际经过哪条路由。如果要在正式使用前确认配置是否合格，请使用只读权限的临时文件夹，测试一个无害的本地工具任务及其后续轮次。</p> <p><a id=\"supported-models\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">支持的模型</h2> <p>Bedrock Runtime 提供方使用推理配置文件 ID；Bedrock Mantle 提供方使用模型 ID。所选模型或配置文件必须在你的 AWS 区域中可用，并且你的 AWS 身份有权访问。</p> <p><a id=\"global-and-geo-cross-region-inference-using-the-bedrock-runtime-endpoint\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"bedrock-runtime-global-geo\">使用 Bedrock Runtime 端点进行 Global 和 Geo 跨区域推理</h3> <p>Global CRIS 可以将请求路由到全球受支持的商业 AWS 区域；Geo CRIS 则会将请求路由到配置文件所属地理区域内。</p> <p>请选择符合 AWS 权限和数据驻留要求的路由范围。</p> <p>将 <code>model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock-runtime\"</code> 与可选的 <code>model</code> 配置配合使用，并将其设置为以下列表中的推理配置文件 ID。该提供方使用 <code>https://bedrock-runtime.{region}.amazonaws.com/openai/v1</code>, 其中 <code>{region}</code> 是你发送请求所使用的受支持源 AWS 区域。Global 和 Geo CRIS 使用相同的端点地址。</p> <h4 id=\"global-cris\">Global CRIS</h4> <p>支持的模型和推理配置文件 ID：</p> <ul> <li>GPT-6 Astra：<code>global.openai.gpt-6-astra</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Sol：<code>global.openai.gpt-6-sol</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Luna：<code>global.openai.gpt-6-luna</code></li> </ul> <p>以下示例在 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 中使用 Global CRIS 配置 Astra：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock-runtime\"\nmodel = \"global.openai.gpt-6-astra\"\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"united-states-geo-cris\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"geo-cris\">美国 Geo CRIS</h4> <p>支持的模型和推理配置文件 ID：</p> <ul> <li>GPT-6 Astra：<code>us.openai.gpt-6-astra</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Sol：<code>us.openai.gpt-6-sol</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Luna：<code>us.openai.gpt-6-luna</code></li> </ul> <p>Codex 内置的 Runtime 模型选择器列出美国 Geo 和 Global 变体。</p> <p>模型和 CRIS 的可用情况会因源 AWS 区域而异。选择提供方和模型之前，请查看 AWS 的<a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-profiles-support.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">推理配置文件支持的区域和模型（需联网）</a>（该页面会链接到各模型的确切推理配置文件 ID 和区域可用性），以及 AWS 的<a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-region-compatibility.html#model-regions-openai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">按模型查看区域可用性（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"in-region-inference-using-the-bedrock-mantle-endpoint\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"bedrock-mantle\">使用 Bedrock Mantle 端点进行区域内推理</h3> <p>将 <code>model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock\"</code> 与可选的模型 ID 配合使用。该提供方使用 <code>https://bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws/openai/v1</code>。</p> <p>支持的模型和模型 ID：</p> <ul> <li>GPT-6 Astra：<code>openai.gpt-6-astra</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Sol：<code>openai.gpt-6-sol</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Luna：<code>openai.gpt-6-luna</code></li> </ul> <p>GPT-6 Sol 和 Luna 目前可通过 Mantle 在 <code>us-east-1</code>（北弗吉尼亚）使用。模型可用情况会因 AWS 区域而异。选择提供方和模型之前，请查看 AWS 的<a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-region-compatibility.html#model-regions-openai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">按模型查看区域可用性（需联网）</a>。GPT-6 Astra 的详情请参阅 <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-6-astra.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bedrock 上的 GPT-6 Astra 模型页面（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"feature-availability\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">功能可用性</h2> <p>此配置适用于本地 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 工作流程。目前不能使用网页端托管的 ChatGPT Work、Codex 云端功能，以及依赖 OpenAI 托管云服务或云端管理发现的功能。Runtime 不提供托管网页搜索；如果需要网页搜索，请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=use-mantle-for-hosted-web-search\">Mantle</a>。</p> <p>Codex Security CLI 使用独立的提供方配置。请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">Amazon Bedrock 设置说明</a>配置，不要套用上面的原生客户端设置。</p> <p>Amazon Bedrock 不支持 Fast Mode。Fast Mode 使用优先级处理；而 Amazon Bedrock 当前的初始方案仅支持按需推理。</p> <p><strong>详细功能可用性</strong></p> <p><a id=\"access-and-surfaces\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_11\">访问入口与客户端</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>功能</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669\">网页端 ChatGPT Work</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex 云端</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Work 或 Codex</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">Codex Security CLI</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-c7af5bbd57109077\">IDE 扩展</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-e3c5173f4c4c14ef\">Codex SDK、<code>codex exec</code> 和脚本化工作流</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"models-and-multimodal\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_12\">模型与多模态</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>功能</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">由 Bedrock 托管推理的受支持 OpenAI 模型</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583\">快速模式（Fast Mode）</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">图像生成与编辑</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=use-voice-dictation\">语音听写</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\">Runtime 上的托管网页搜索</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"local-features\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_13\">本地功能</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>功能</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security 插件与本地扫描</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=do-a-local-code-review\">使用 <code>/review</code> 进行本地代码审查</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-f464374c0d895ab1\">审批请求的自动审查</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-4d7a5dc78b3c591e\">沙箱与权限控制</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">项目级和独立的计划任务</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">计划任务</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">工作树与内置 Git 工具</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">本地环境与可重复执行的操作</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-c302b8efa03eab38\">Appshots</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"browser-and-remote-control\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_14\">浏览器与远程控制</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>功能</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">内置浏览器预览与评论</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/browser?surface=app#app-computer-use-in-the-browser\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在浏览器中使用 Computer Use（计算机操作）（需联网）</a></td> <td><code>有限制</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">通过 Chrome 使用 ChatGPT</a></td> <td><code>有限制</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use（计算机操作）</a></td> <td><code>有限制</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=connect-to-an-ssh-host\">SSH 远程连接</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f\">移动设备远程控制</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"customization-and-extensions\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_15\">自定义与扩展</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>功能</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">使用 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 编写自定义指令</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">技能</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>（插件功能受限）</td> <td><code>有限制</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">共享插件</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">连接器</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">子智能体与自定义智能体</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a></td> <td><code>有限制</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">Computer History（计算机历史）</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"cloud-and-integrations\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_16\">云端与集成</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>功能</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex 云端聊天</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites（网站）</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641?anchor=give-codex-other-tasks\">通过 <code>@codex</code> 委派 GitHub issue 和 PR</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">GitHub 代码审查与自动 PR 审查</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444\">Slack 云端集成</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-434ee24ee096022e\">Linear 云端集成</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"admin-security-and-analytics\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_17\">管理、安全与分析</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>功能</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">SAML SSO、MFA 和工作区用户管理</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\"><code>requirements.toml</code> 托管配置</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=cloud-managed-requirements\">云端管理的配置策略</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">ChatGPT 工作区 RBAC 和自定义角色</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4?anchor=enterprise-grade-security-and-privacy\">SCIM、EKM 与域名验证</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4?anchor=enterprise-grade-security-and-privacy\">企业级数据保留与数据驻留控制</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://openai.com/business-data/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">默认不使用 API 或商业数据训练（需联网）</a></td> <td><code>可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">分析仪表板</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">分析 API</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">合规 API 与审计日志</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">面向已连接 GitHub 仓库的 Codex Security 云端功能</a></td> <td><code>不可用</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <div id=\"codex-plan-region-limits\"><sup>*</sup> 此功能目前仅在特定区域开放。区域限制请参阅相应功能文档。</div> <div id=\"codex-plan-plugin-limits\"><sup>†</sup> 可使用本地插件包，以及无需 ChatGPT 身份验证的 OpenAI 精选插件（包括 Codex Security）。需要 ChatGPT 身份验证的插件、连接器或云端托管的共享功能不可用。</div> <p><a id=\"troubleshooting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_18\">故障排查</h2> <p>如果设置失败，请检查以下事项：</p> <ul> <li>模型 ID 是否与受支持模型完全一致。</li> <li>端点是否使用了正确的模型提供方：Runtime 端点使用 <code>amazon-bedrock-runtime</code>；Mantle 端点使用 <code>amazon-bedrock</code>。</li> <li>是否指定了模型可用的 AWS 区域。</li> <li>Bedrock API 密钥或 AWS 凭证是否有效且未过期。</li> <li>AWS 身份是否有权访问所选 Bedrock 模型。</li> <li><code>AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK</code> 是否被设置为已过期或非预期的密钥。</li> <li>对于桌面应用或 IDE 扩展，所需环境变量是否存在于 <code>~/.codex/.env</code> 中。</li> </ul> <p>如果使用 AWS SDK 配置文件进行身份验证，请运行 <code>aws sts get-caller-identity --profile codex-bedrock</code>，确认所选配置文件对应的身份。请将 <code>codex-bedrock</code> 替换为你的配置文件名称；使用默认凭据链时，可以省略 <code>--profile</code>。此命令只能确认 AWS 身份，不能证明该身份有权调用 Bedrock 模型。还要单独检查 <code>AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK</code>，以免非预期的 API 密钥选择了另一条身份验证路径。</p> <p><a id=\"support-boundaries\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_19\">支持范围</h2> <p>OpenAI 支持团队可以协助处理 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 客户端设置、配置、本地 CLI 行为、桌面应用行为、IDE 扩展行为以及本地产品体验问题。</p> <p>AWS 凭证、IAM 权限、Bedrock 模型访问权限、配额、账单、区域可用性、Bedrock 请求失败、AWS 服务日志或 Bedrock 服务行为，请联系你的 AWS 管理员或 AWS 支持团队。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"use-chatgpt-work-and-codex-with-amazon-bedrock\">Use ChatGPT Work and Codex with Amazon Bedrock</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Configure local ChatGPT Work and Codex surfaces to use OpenAI models available through Amazon Bedrock. In this setup, the local client sends model requests to Bedrock using AWS-managed authentication and access controls.</p> <p>This page covers direct access to Bedrock. If your organization already provides a model gateway, follow <a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">Use API/provider credentials</a>. To configure a gateway backed by Bedrock, see <a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4\">Bedrock through LiteLLM</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2> <p>When you configure a local ChatGPT Work or Codex surface with Amazon Bedrock as the model provider, the OpenAI-hosted Responses API isn't in the request path. The local client sends model requests to Amazon Bedrock, and Bedrock provides an OpenAI-compatible Responses API implementation for supported OpenAI models.</p> <p>Authentication is AWS-native. Users authenticate with a Bedrock API key or AWS IAM credentials. They do not use ChatGPT sign-in or <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code> for this provider.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Make sure you have:</p> <ul> <li>Credentials for the AWS account you want to use.</li> <li>Access to supported OpenAI models in Amazon Bedrock.</li> <li>Access to an AWS Region where the selected model is available.</li> <li>AWS permission to invoke the selected model or inference profile.</li> </ul> <p>Check the model-specific IAM requirements. For example, GPT-6 Sol through Runtime also requires <code>bedrock:InvokeModel</code> on the account's default project. See AWS's <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-6-sol.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GPT-6 Sol setup instructions (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"configure-the-provider\">Configure the provider</h2> <p>Codex allows you to configure the provider by setting <code>model_provider</code> in <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>. The ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, IDE extension, and SDK read the same local configuration layers.</p> <p>Choose the provider for the Amazon Bedrock endpoint you want to use: Bedrock Runtime for cross-Region inference (CRIS), or Bedrock Mantle for in-Region inference.</p> <p>Use Bedrock Runtime for new configurations:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock-runtime\"\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n</code></pre> <p>Hosted web search isn't available on Bedrock Runtime. If you need it, use <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=use-mantle-for-hosted-web-search\">Bedrock Mantle</a>. The <code>amazon-bedrock</code> provider selects Mantle; <code>amazon-bedrock-runtime</code> selects Runtime.</p> <h3 id=\"use-mantle-for-hosted-web-search\">Use Mantle for hosted web search</h3> <p>For the Bedrock Mantle endpoint:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock\"\nweb_search = \"cached\"\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"choose-a-model\">Choose a model</h3> <p>Codex uses the configured <code>model_provider</code> to choose which models appear in the model picker: models supported through the Bedrock Runtime endpoint for <code>amazon-bedrock-runtime</code>, or through the Bedrock Mantle endpoint for <code>amazon-bedrock</code>.</p> <p>You can optionally specify a <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=supported-models\">supported model</a> in the configuration file. The built-in provider supplies its own model catalog. When switching endpoints, change the provider and any explicit model ID together.</p> <p>Model availability varies by AWS Region. Refer to AWS <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-region-compatibility.html#model-regions-openai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Regional availability by models (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"authentication-options\">Authentication options</h2> <p>Local ChatGPT Work and Codex surfaces support two Bedrock authentication paths. They check them in this order:</p> <ol> <li>Bedrock API key.</li> <li>AWS SDK credential chain.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"option-1-bedrock-api-key\">Option 1: Bedrock API key</h3> <p>Set the Bedrock API key in the environment the local client reads. You must specify a Region when using API-key authentication.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">export AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=&lt;your-bedrock-api-key&gt;\nexport AWS_REGION=us-east-2\n</code></pre> <p>On Windows PowerShell:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">$env:AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK = \"&lt;your-bedrock-api-key&gt;\"\n$env:AWS_REGION = \"us-east-2\"\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"option-2-aws-sdk-credentials\">Option 2: AWS SDK credentials</h3> <p>Use this path when your organization manages Bedrock access through the AWS SDK credential chain. The local client can use these standard AWS SDK credential sources:</p> <h4 id=\"shared-aws-configuration-files\">Shared AWS configuration files</h4> <p>Configure the shared AWS <code>config</code> and <code>credentials</code> files:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">aws configure\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"environment-variables\">Environment variables</h4> <p>Set the standard AWS SDK credential environment variables:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=&lt;your-access-key-id&gt;\nexport AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=&lt;your-secret-access-key&gt;\nexport AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=&lt;your-session-token&gt;\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"aws-management-console-credentials\">AWS Management Console credentials</h4> <p>Log in with AWS Management Console credentials:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">aws login\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"aws-sso-or-a-named-profile\">AWS SSO or a named profile</h4> <p>Log in with AWS SSO and select the named profile:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">aws sso login --profile codex-bedrock\nexport AWS_PROFILE=codex-bedrock\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"federated-identity\">Federated identity</h4> <p>For corporate SSO or OIDC federation, configure a federated identity with <code>credential_process</code> outside the local client and let the AWS SDK resolve credentials. Put browser login, token exchange, caching, and refresh in your AWS profile's <code>credential_process</code> helper.</p> <h2 id=\"desktop-app-and-ide-extension\">Desktop app and IDE extension</h2> <p>Desktop apps and IDE extensions may not inherit environment variables from the shell. Put required values in <code>~/.codex/.env</code>, then restart the app or extension. On Windows, the default path is <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\.env</code>.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">export AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=&lt;your-bedrock-api-key&gt;\nexport AWS_REGION=us-east-2\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"verify-setup\">Verify setup</h2> <ul> <li>In Codex CLI, open <code>/status</code> and confirm the model provider matches your endpoint: <code>amazon-bedrock</code> for Mantle in-Region inference, or <code>amazon-bedrock-runtime</code> for Runtime Global or Geo cross-Region inference.</li> <li>In the ChatGPT desktop app, select Work or Codex and start a new task after restarting the app.</li> <li>In the IDE extension, start a new session after restarting the extension.</li> <li>Confirm the selected model is available in the configured AWS Region and that the AWS identity has permission to access it.</li> </ul> <p>Then send a short prompt in a new task:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Reply with exactly: bedrock-ok\n</code></pre> <p>Expect <code>bedrock-ok</code>. Confirm the provider and model in the client; the reply alone doesn't identify the route. For rollout qualification, use a disposable folder with read-only permissions and verify a harmless local tool task and a follow-up turn.</p> <h2 id=\"supported-models\">Supported models</h2> <p>Use an inference profile ID for Bedrock Runtime provider or a model ID for Bedrock Mantle provider. The selected model or profile must be available in your AWS Region and accessible to your AWS identity.</p> <h3 id=\"global-and-geo-cross-region-inference-using-the-bedrock-runtime-endpoint\">Global and Geo cross-Region inference using the Bedrock Runtime endpoint</h3> <p>Global CRIS can route requests to supported commercial AWS Regions worldwide, whereas Geo CRIS routes requests within the profile's geography. Choose a routing scope that meets your AWS permissions and data-residency requirements.</p> <p>Use <code>model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock-runtime\"</code> with the optional <code>model</code> configuration set to an inference profile ID from the following lists. The provider uses <code>https://bedrock-runtime.{region}.amazonaws.com/openai/v1</code>, where <code>{region}</code> is the supported source AWS Region from which you send requests. Both Global and Geo CRIS use this endpoint address.</p> <h4 id=\"global-cris\">Global CRIS</h4> <p>Supported models and inference profile IDs:</p> <ul> <li>GPT-6 Astra: <code>global.openai.gpt-6-astra</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Sol: <code>global.openai.gpt-6-sol</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Luna: <code>global.openai.gpt-6-luna</code></li> </ul> <p>For example, configure Astra with Global CRIS in <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock-runtime\"\nmodel = \"global.openai.gpt-6-astra\"\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"united-states-geo-cris\">United States Geo CRIS</h4> <p>Supported models and inference profile IDs:</p> <ul> <li>GPT-6 Astra: <code>us.openai.gpt-6-astra</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Sol: <code>us.openai.gpt-6-sol</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Luna: <code>us.openai.gpt-6-luna</code></li> </ul> <p>Codex's built-in Runtime model picker lists the United States Geo and Global variants.</p> <p>Model and CRIS availability vary by source AWS Region. See AWS <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-profiles-support.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Supported Regions and models for inference profiles (online)</a>, which links to each model's exact inference profile IDs and regional availability, and AWS <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-region-compatibility.html#model-regions-openai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Regional availability by models (online)</a> before selecting a provider and a model.</p> <h3 id=\"in-region-inference-using-the-bedrock-mantle-endpoint\">In-Region inference using the Bedrock Mantle endpoint</h3> <p>Use <code>model_provider = \"amazon-bedrock\"</code> with an optional model ID. The provider uses <code>https://bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws/openai/v1</code>.</p> <p>Supported models and model IDs:</p> <ul> <li>GPT-6 Astra: <code>openai.gpt-6-astra</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Sol: <code>openai.gpt-6-sol</code></li> <li>GPT-6 Luna: <code>openai.gpt-6-luna</code></li> </ul> <p>GPT-6 Sol and Luna are available through Mantle in <code>us-east-1</code> (N. Virginia). Model availability varies by AWS Region. See AWS <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-region-compatibility.html#model-regions-openai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Regional availability by models (online)</a> before selecting a provider and a model. For GPT-6 Astra, refer to the <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-6-astra.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bedrock model page for GPT-6 Astra (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"feature-availability\">Feature availability</h2> <p>This configuration supports local ChatGPT Work and Codex workflows. Hosted ChatGPT Work on the web, Codex cloud, and features that depend on OpenAI-hosted cloud services or cloud-managed discovery aren't currently available. Hosted web search is unavailable on Runtime; use <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=use-mantle-for-hosted-web-search\">Mantle</a> if you need it.</p> <p>Codex Security CLI uses its own provider configuration. Follow its <a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34\">Amazon Bedrock setup</a> rather than the native client settings above.</p> <p>Fast Mode isn't available with Amazon Bedrock. Fast Mode uses priority processing, and the initial Amazon Bedrock offering supports on-demand inference only.</p> <p><a id=\"detailed-feature-availability\"></a> <strong>Detailed feature availability</strong></p> <h4 id=\"access-and-surfaces\">Access and surfaces</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Feature</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669\">ChatGPT Work on the web</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT Work or Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">Codex Security CLI</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-c7af5bbd57109077\">IDE extension</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-e3c5173f4c4c14ef\">Codex SDK, <code>codex exec</code>, and scriptable workflows</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h4 id=\"models-and-multimodal\">Models and multimodal</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Feature</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">Bedrock-backed inference with supported OpenAI models</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583\">Fast mode</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">Image generation and editing</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=use-voice-dictation\">Voice dictation</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\">Hosted web search on Runtime</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h4 id=\"local-features\">Local features</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Feature</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">Codex Security plugin and local scans</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=do-a-local-code-review\">Local code review with <code>/review</code></a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-f464374c0d895ab1\">Auto-review for approval requests</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-4d7a5dc78b3c591e\">Sandboxing and permission controls</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Project and standalone scheduled tasks</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">Worktrees and built-in Git tools</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">Local environments and repeatable actions</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-c302b8efa03eab38\">Appshots</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h4 id=\"browser-and-remote-control\">Browser and remote control</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Feature</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">Built-in browser previews and comments</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/browser?surface=app#app-computer-use-in-the-browser\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Computer Use in the browser (online)</a></td> <td><code>limited</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-a7459570776840aa\">Use ChatGPT with Chrome</a></td> <td><code>limited</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a></td> <td><code>limited</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=connect-to-an-ssh-host\">SSH remote connections</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f\">Mobile remote control</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h4 id=\"customization-and-extensions\">Customization and extensions</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Feature</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">Custom instructions with <code>AGENTS.md</code></a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Skills</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a> (<code>limitedFootnote=plugins</code>)</td> <td><code>limited</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Plugin sharing</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Connectors</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">Subagents and custom agents</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">Memories</a></td> <td><code>limited</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">Computer History</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h4 id=\"cloud-and-integrations\">Cloud and integrations</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Feature</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud chats</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641?anchor=give-codex-other-tasks\">GitHub issue and PR delegation with <code>@codex</code></a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">GitHub code review and automatic PR reviews</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444\">Slack cloud integration</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-434ee24ee096022e\">Linear cloud integration</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h4 id=\"admin-security-and-analytics\">Admin, security, and analytics</h4> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Feature</th> <th>Amazon Bedrock</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">SAML SSO, MFA, and workspace user management</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\"><code>requirements.toml</code> managed config</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=cloud-managed-requirements\">Cloud-managed config policies</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">ChatGPT workspace RBAC and custom roles</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4?anchor=enterprise-grade-security-and-privacy\">SCIM, EKM, and domain verification</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4?anchor=enterprise-grade-security-and-privacy\">Enterprise retention and residency controls</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://openai.com/business-data/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">No training on API or business data by default (online)</a></td> <td><code>available</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Analytics dashboard</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API and audit logs</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Codex Security cloud for connected GitHub repositories</a></td> <td><code>unavailable</code></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <div id=\"codex-plan-region-limits\"><sup>*</sup> Feature is currently limited to only specific regions. Check the individual feature documentation to learn more about regional restrictions.</div> <div id=\"codex-plan-plugin-limits\"><sup>†</sup> Local plugin bundles and OpenAI-curated plugins that don't require ChatGPT authentication, including Codex Security, are available. Plugins that require ChatGPT authentication, connectors, or cloud-hosted sharing aren't available.</div> <h2 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h2> <p>If setup fails, check the following:</p> <ul> <li>The model ID exactly matches a supported model.</li> <li>You use the correct model provider for the endpoint: <code>amazon-bedrock-runtime</code> for Runtime endpoint or <code>amazon-bedrock</code> for Mantle endpoint.</li> <li>You specify an AWS Region where the model is available.</li> <li>The Bedrock API key or AWS credentials are valid and not expired.</li> <li>The AWS identity has permission to access the selected Bedrock model.</li> <li><code>AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK</code> isn't set to an expired or unintended key.</li> <li>For desktop app or IDE extension usage, required environment variables are present in <code>~/.codex/.env</code>.</li> </ul> <p>For AWS SDK profile authentication, run <code>aws sts get-caller-identity --profile codex-bedrock</code> to confirm the identity for your selected profile. Replace <code>codex-bedrock</code> with your profile name, or omit <code>--profile</code> when using the default credential chain. This checks AWS identity, not permission to invoke a Bedrock model. Check <code>AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK</code> separately so an unintended API key doesn't select a different authentication path.</p> <h2 id=\"support-boundaries\">Support boundaries</h2> <p>OpenAI Support can help with ChatGPT Work and Codex client setup, configuration, local CLI behavior, desktop app behavior, IDE extension behavior, and the local product experience.</p> <p>For AWS credentials, IAM permissions, Bedrock model access, quotas, billing, regional availability, Bedrock request failures, AWS service logs, or Bedrock service behavior, contact the customer's AWS administrator or AWS Support.</p>"};
